on, category, reference, amount, tax status)\n- ✅ **CT-21**: Dashboard and tax summary accuracies with correct calculations\n- ✅ **CT-22**: Chart axis labels provide sufficient precision for non-zero amounts\n\n### Failing Tests (4)\n**Constraints (Failing):**\n- ❌ **CS-15**: Date range validation - Invalid date ranges (start > end) are not rejected with error; system simply shows \"No transactions found\"\n- ❌ **CS-23**: Missing category validation - Transactions can be created without a category; system allows blank category assignments\n- ❌ **CS-24**: Category deletion protection - Deleting a category with assigned transactions is allowed, leaving those transactions with blank category fields instead of blocking deletion or requiring reassignment\n\n### Key Findings\nThe application demonstrates **solid core functionality** with effective transaction management, categorization, filtering, and reporting. However, there are **critical validation gaps** in category management and date range handling that should be addressed to prevent data integrity issues and poor user experience."
